From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saif <saifuddin.kaijar@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 11:34:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] xilinx-ai-engine: Granularize error handling init options

Refactor the AIE partition initialization sequence and clean up lock
usage following the granularization of error-handling init options:

- Remove the now-redundant monolithic aie_error_handling_init(),
  aie2ps_error_handling_init(), aie2ps_priv_error_handling_init(),
  aie_group_error_init(), and aie_group_error_init_loc() functions from
  ai-engine-interrupt.c.  Callers now invoke the three fine-grained
  entry points directly (aie2ps_error_handling_init_shim,
  aie2ps_error_handling_init_mem_aie, aie_config_error_halt_event) so
  the umbrella wrappers are dead code.

- Drop the aie_error_handling_init() declaration from
  ai-engine-internal.h accordingly.

- Add aie_aperture_iowrite32_nolock() — a bare iowrite32 wrapper for
  call sites that already hold read_lock(&aperture->reset_lock).  Use
  it in aie_event_bc_block() to acquire the lock once around all four
  directional writes instead of re-acquiring it per write.

- Refactor aie2ps_error_handling_init_shim(): only set up L1 control
  and L2 enable for the lead column (start_col + 1); all columns
  still get aie_group_error_init_shim().

- Add IRQ CPU-affinity support in ai-engine-part.c:
    * New module parameter aie_irq_cpu (default -1, no affinity).
    * irq_set_affinity_hint() called after request_irq() and cleared
      in aie_part_release() to ensure clean teardown.

- Fix handshake update path in aie_partition_handshake_update(): flush
  pending PM ops after writing the handshake region.

- Remove the inline flush-and-retry logic from
  AIE_PART_INIT_OPT_HANDSHAKE handling in aie_part_pm_ops(); that
  flush now happens explicitly at the call sites.

- Refactor aie2ps_part_initialize() in ai-engine-reset.c:
    * Introduce a flush_out error label so that any failure in the
      PM-ops-queuing phase still drains the queue before returning.
    * Batch non-data pm_ops (column reset, shim reset, block NOC AXI
      MM error, enable column clock buffer, zeroize mem, UC mem priv)
      into a single aie_part_pm_ops() call with flush=0 rather than
      multiple flushing calls.
    * Clear the DMA-pause bits from init_opts after the poll succeeds
      so they are not re-submitted in subsequent pm_ops batches.
    * Move ISOLATE handling to after aie_part_request_tiles() since
      that function flushes pm_ops internally; isolation uses direct
      iowrite32 paths and does not need to be queued.
    * Reorder SET_L2_IRQ and HANDSHAKE after NMU_CONFIG to match the
      hardware sequencing requirement; add missing error check on
      aie2ps_part_write_handshake().

Signed-off-by: Saif <saifuddin.kaijar@amd.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
